     "0X" prefix, and the number will be read in base 16; if [4mbase[24m is zero or 2, the string may then  in‐
     clude a "0b" or "0B" prefix, and the number will be read in base 2; otherwise, a zero [4mbase[24m is taken
     as 10 (decimal) unless the next character is '0', in which case it is taken as 8 (octal).

